{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2746 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "915c28ab18530852ff473feed262b070af12f04cde67279d17b692f4e498bd3b" :edb/db-before-t 2745 :edb/db-after-t 2746 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536058 50 #inst "2026-10-09T13:57:12.166Z" 13194139536058 true] [17592186129065 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381414 13194139536058 true] [17592186129066 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381421 13194139536058 true] [17592186129090 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381428 13194139536058 true] [17592186129148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381400 13194139536058 true] [17592186129148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381407 13194139536058 true] [17592186381400 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381401 13194139536058 true] [17592186381400 1089 "q-97061" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381400 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536058 true] [17592186381400 1100 "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $B$ to basis $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$\n- $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381400 1113 #uuid "1f150370-b1b6-505a-ba94-e0bab21cf5b3" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381400 1145 "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075067/assets/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381401 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381402 13194139536058 true] [17592186381401 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381403 13194139536058 true] [17592186381401 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381404 13194139536058 true] [17592186381401 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381405 13194139536058 true] [17592186381401 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381406 13194139536058 true] [17592186381401 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536058 true] [17592186381401 1041 "selection" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381401 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381403 13194139536058 true] [17592186381401 1110 #uuid "b946ca2e-a0be-58df-8c67-d7d144572d42" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381402 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381402 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536058 true] [17592186381402 1111 #uuid "f2c7506f-f7fa-5df3-8aff-9fcecef6f899" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381403 1034 "I only" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381403 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536058 true] [17592186381403 1111 #uuid "cb0207db-3fc1-575c-94d4-0f4ef2869c92" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381404 1034 "III only" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381404 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536058 true] [17592186381404 1111 #uuid "074e22a5-4373-50c3-a85d-78d4fb8eb19e" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381405 1034 "I and II only" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381405 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536058 true] [17592186381405 1111 #uuid "e3d6c433-c78e-53b3-aaa1-c5b29247f3c7" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381406 1034 "II only" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381406 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536058 true] [17592186381406 1111 #uuid "68c9106d-0401-5492-b391-5ab9738629a3" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381407 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381408 13194139536058 true] [17592186381407 1089 "q-97065" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381407 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536058 true] [17592186381407 1100 "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $C$ to basis $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}$\n- $[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381407 1113 #uuid "bef25f3b-1e7c-5482-8293-7458030a7ccb" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381407 1145 "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075067/assets/9ba3d1f0eebdfc82c40f36bdbe16896ca15516b623c695b72c331861955329bc.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381408 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381409 13194139536058 true] [17592186381408 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381410 13194139536058 true] [17592186381408 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381411 13194139536058 true] [17592186381408 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381412 13194139536058 true] [17592186381408 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381413 13194139536058 true] [17592186381408 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536058 true] [17592186381408 1041 "selection" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381408 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381409 13194139536058 true] [17592186381408 1110 #uuid "45ed16fd-024f-549a-9543-f16d0ed45d42" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381409 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381409 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536058 true] [17592186381409 1111 #uuid "ea5211ea-d872-551f-8ce0-a9d56c4131f3" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381410 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381410 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536058 true] [17592186381410 1111 #uuid "9180f9e7-022d-55c4-b03a-55ac0208007c" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381411 1034 "I only" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381411 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536058 true] [17592186381411 1111 #uuid "8d402afc-010f-5981-94fa-2b21233221b7" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381412 1034 "III only" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381412 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536058 true] [17592186381412 1111 #uuid "e4152d3d-3ea6-5a95-98be-a59cf5237d41" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381413 1034 "II only" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381413 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536058 true] [17592186381413 1111 #uuid "a4ea98fb-3bf3-5522-8867-f097e3600b38" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381414 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381415 13194139536058 true] [17592186381414 1089 "q-97112" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381414 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536058 true] [17592186381414 1100 "$$\n[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381414 1113 #uuid "8a321cf1-158f-55e2-bafd-86ca358cc708" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381414 1145 "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075067/assets/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381415 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381416 13194139536058 true] [17592186381415 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381417 13194139536058 true] [17592186381415 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381418 13194139536058 true] [17592186381415 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381419 13194139536058 true] [17592186381415 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381420 13194139536058 true] [17592186381415 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536058 true] [17592186381415 1041 "selection" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381415 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381418 13194139536058 true] [17592186381415 1110 #uuid "a94f7caf-1d10-5724-a037-b750a6008bfa" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381416 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381416 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536058 true] [17592186381416 1111 #uuid "fa8dc33d-7d3a-5ec9-a4bc-50fd64786298" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381417 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -8 & -11\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381417 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536058 true] [17592186381417 1111 #uuid "d2a76fb6-d182-56f0-9acc-9177276d9fcf" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381418 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381418 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536058 true] [17592186381418 1111 #uuid "c0882bae-cba6-5a08-80ac-05f48357761e" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381419 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -7\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381419 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536058 true] [17592186381419 1111 #uuid "19dd9573-e707-5ec2-9bf7-52e7597336c4" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381420 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}15 & -5 \\\\ -10 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381420 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536058 true] [17592186381420 1111 #uuid "aeeba22d-5626-5997-a7e4-4f1541b482de" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381421 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381422 13194139536058 true] [17592186381421 1089 "q-97121" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381421 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536058 true] [17592186381421 1100 "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381421 1113 #uuid "3a316dac-2644-5b90-b954-acca3323828e" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381421 1145 "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075067/assets/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381423 13194139536058 true] [17592186381422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381424 13194139536058 true] [17592186381422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381425 13194139536058 true] [17592186381422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381426 13194139536058 true] [17592186381422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381427 13194139536058 true] [17592186381422 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536058 true] [17592186381422 1041 "selection" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381422 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381423 13194139536058 true] [17592186381422 1110 #uuid "dcdde292-5d0a-5633-bdf1-7267caca39e4" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381423 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381423 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536058 true] [17592186381423 1111 #uuid "e8675898-6a2a-5953-a0a9-8a1243afd6bc" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381424 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}11 & -8 \\\\ -16 & 11\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381424 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536058 true] [17592186381424 1111 #uuid "b80043ef-a3f7-5a72-a33e-75aeedc12272" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381425 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -5\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381425 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536058 true] [17592186381425 1111 #uuid "4153e90f-7e6a-5609-bc62-6edb949cbace" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381426 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}9 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381426 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536058 true] [17592186381426 1111 #uuid "befe0a30-923b-5a00-aaf4-c7b0aae61a89" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381427 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-13 & -4 \\\\ -7 & -11\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381427 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536058 true] [17592186381427 1111 #uuid "09f060f3-f27c-5631-b843-bb5ab8ff867e" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381428 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381429 13194139536058 true] [17592186381428 1089 "q-97282" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381428 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536058 true] [17592186381428 1100 "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]},\\,C={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2},$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$, shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381428 1113 #uuid "99a4cf6e-01fc-5011-bfec-d4d90bdff4c8" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381428 1145 "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075067/assets/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nFirst, let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of vectors from $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ To do this, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination until we get the identity matrix on the left. By doing this, we obtain the required change-of-coordinates matrix on the right.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot (-1)-3\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381429 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381430 13194139536058 true] [17592186381429 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381431 13194139536058 true] [17592186381429 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381432 13194139536058 true] [17592186381429 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381433 13194139536058 true] [17592186381429 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381434 13194139536058 true] [17592186381429 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536058 true] [17592186381429 1041 "selection" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381429 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381432 13194139536058 true] [17592186381429 1110 #uuid "d363fc71-e9cc-505b-a190-c86887830854" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381430 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381430 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536058 true] [17592186381430 1111 #uuid "c4bb209d-cf52-57ca-90d0-620ac03535d2" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381431 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}6 & -7 \\\\ 8 & -7\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381431 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536058 true] [17592186381431 1111 #uuid "25008b87-14ae-504d-b403-975779bf265c" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381432 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381432 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536058 true] [17592186381432 1111 #uuid "8656bc73-cc3b-55f6-9ddb-137eb59c3c52" 13194139536058 true] [17592186381433 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}11 & 9 \\\\ 8 & 11\\end{alig